  "notes": [
    "Four independent successful launches each present and independently verify three screen frames through the Windows-registered adapter. The first three launch variants clear primary colors; the fourth renders an alpha-pattern blend through the actual UMD/OpenVINO CPU provider into the swap-chain back buffer.",
    "The first two cases use the same executable with Hidden and Normal startup respectively. Both pass. The awake case explicitly holds ES_DISPLAY_REQUIRED and reports a visible, nonminimized, uncloaked HWND despite startup_show=0. Thus hidden startup is not an observed cause of failure in this package.",
    "The UMD now returns DXGI_STATUS_NO_REDIRECTION as required without shared D3D9 hardware. v41 lacked that return status, and did not capture instantaneous window/display visibility. This is not a controlled A/B attribution isolating that status from every environmental difference.",
    "The screen oracle uses GDI only to measure pixels after DWM flushes; it does not deliver the test frames. The normal desktop and DWM remain active on the original display path.",
    "The final NPU-only draw request fails because the guest runtime has no NPU device. It completes zero inference operations and zero presents with no CPU fallback or resource leaks. The physical NPU component evidence is separate.",
    "Twenty-five kernel CPU-worker fences complete: twelve successful presentation copies, twelve clears for successful cases, and one clear before the rejected NPU request. Shader CPU inference is counted separately. No performance claim follows from these functional tests."
  ],
